"dram_pm_suspend" — "drm_pm_suspend" not found in i915_driver.c? Interesting. In the latest kernel (6.x), `i915_pm_suspend` calls `i915_drm_suspend(&i915->drm)` directly, without using `dev_pm_ops` on the DRM bus. In other words, this kernel tree is a newer one (around 6.9, post the commit "drm: Drop drm bus..."). Indeed, in 6.9 there was no call to `drm_pm_suspend`, and `i915_pm_suspend` looks like:

```
static int i915_pm_suspend(struct device *kdev)
{
	struct drm_i915_private *i915 = dev_get_drvdata(kdev);

	intel_runtime_pm_get(i915);

	return i915_drm_suspend(&i915->drm);
}
```

